g{\"name\": name, \"email\": email})\n}\n\nNeed refactor. External behavior identical: status codes, response bodies. Note original success response: Content-Type application/json, body JSON object with name/email plus trailing newline from Encoder. Error responses: no Content-Type set, body exact strings no newline. Need preserve. If we use helper writeJSON? For errors, if we set Content-Type? That would change headers, not body/status. User says same status codes, same response bodies. Headers maybe not explicitly but external behavior likely includes headers? Keep identical: errors no Content-Type. Success Content-Type set. Could use writeError(w, status, message) that writes status and exact bytes. For success, writeUserJSON sets header and encodes map. Need ensure JSON encoding identical: map[string]string{\"name\": name, \"email\": email}. Go json encodes map keys sorted alphabetically: email then name. Original same. Encoder adds newline. If we use json.Marshal and w.Write, no newline, body differs. So use json.NewEncoder(w).Encode or ensure newline. Better helper encodeJSON(w, v) sets Content-Type and uses Encoder.", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0010547834681347013], [22916, -7.922609329223633]], [[1144, -1.609338323760312e-05], [513, -12.26286792755127]], [[4087, -0.015840519219636917], [310, -4.425577163696289]], [[1156, -0.025367729365825653], [303, -4.067388534545898]], [[579, -0.2916777431964874], [25, -2.1540491580963135]], [[1622, -0.002818081062287092], [3296, -6.8081865310668945]], [[13, -0.41083791851997375], [25, -1.3900822401046753]], [[14235, -0.03274698555469513], [1165, -4.0901312828063965]], [[89109, -0.26470816135406494], [7936, -1.9742532968521118]], [[5805, -0.00020726682851091027], [2400, -8.94631290435791]], [[9830, -0.027385909110307693], [6795, -3.6702234745025635]], [[6795, -3.254466719226912e-05], [17369, -11.874256134033203]], [[47781, -1.378651738166809], [1083, -1.62372887134552]], [[4475, -0.9830129146575928], [2833, -1.096933126449585]],